  "raw_text": "# BROWN & WILLIAMSON TOBACCO CORPORATION\n\n# RESEARCH & DEVELOPMENT\n\n# INTERNAL CORRESPONDENCE\n\nTO: MR. P. H. HARPER\n\nCC: MR. T. E. SANDFUR DR. P. L. AULBACH\n\nFROM: MR. D. S. ROTH\n\nDATE: JANUARY 13, 1983\n\nSUBJECT: KENT 80/KS TAR REDUCTION - FINLAND/907\n\nRef S/R 107/82\n\nAfter evaluations and rejections of tar reduction samples 49B, 50B, and 51B we have reviewed deliveries and designs of several KENT products to find one which meets the \\(10.0 \\mathrm{mg / c i g}\\) . (DPM) and \\(0.7 \\mathrm{mg / c i g}\\) . nicotine constraints.\n\nWe propose the following two trials.\n\n<table><tr><td></td><td>Trial 1</td><td>Trial 2</td></tr><tr><td>·Blend (%)</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>MGLF-31</td><td>69.9</td><td>69.9</td></tr><tr><td>Oriental</td><td>10.3</td><td>10.3</td></tr><tr><td>MRT</td><td>5.0</td><td>0.0</td></tr><tr><td>F.C. WTS</td><td>14.8</td><td>19.8</td></tr><tr><td>·Final Casing</td><td>MGE-651</td><td>MGE-651</td></tr><tr><td>·Final Flavor</td><td>MGE-603</td><td>MGE-603</td></tr><tr><td>·Cigarette Paper</td><td>---</td><td>---</td></tr><tr><td>·Density</td><td>---</td><td>---</td></tr><tr><td>·Filter Tow</td><td>---</td><td>KENT GOLDEN LIGHTS (Less 2%)</td></tr><tr><td>·Plugwrap</td><td>---</td><td>9500 Coresta</td></tr><tr><td>·Tipping</td><td>---</td><td>1100 Coresta MMP*</td></tr><tr><td>·Vent Target</td><td>---</td><td>42-44%</td></tr></table>\n\n\\*We recommend the micromechanically perforated tipping because this is the only type of tipping with essentially invisible perforations at this high porosity level.\n\n\n\nDSR/bfw\n\n0014x\n\nJAN 1 8 1983\n\n<table><tr><td>Point</td><td>X</td><td>Y</td></tr><tr><td>D</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>S</td><td>2</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>R</td><td>3</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>4</td><td>1</td></tr></table>",
